From 83d5119428f3d7e10d303280ea2927b0653598a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:51:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(state): recency pages probe messages only for rows that
 can reach the page

list_sessions_rich(order_by_last_active=True) ran the per-session MAX(messages.timestamp)
probe for every admitted row on each sidebar poll miss (~100-140 ms CPU per read on the
hub's 22.5k-session store). hermes_state_recency keeps a per-store cache of each session's
in-window message max, folds in messages past the AUTOINCREMENT watermark inside the read's
own snapshot, and derives the page threshold T from idx_sessions_effective_activity. Only
sessions whose upper bound reaches T (plus their ancestors) enter the exact ranking, so the
page is identical to the unrestricted query; anything unprovable falls back to it.

Hub (read-only, one snapshot): limit=100 page 101.7ms -> 14.3ms CPU, identical rows on 4 shapes.
